      "summary": "A hypothetical 153-point no-three-in-line subset of G_77 cannot have nonidentity rotational symmetry. If a hypothetical 154-point subset has nontrivial rotational symmetry, it must be invariant under the half-turn about (38,38), with the center unselected. These restrictions are not nonexistence results, and general centered-half-turn symmetry is strictly broader than rct4.",
